; UniPrefs text module: lists an existing editor in UniPrefs.
; Copy to Modules/<Name>.module. Hidden while the editor is missing.
; ";" starts a comment. Name, Editor and Categories are required.

; the CLI name (UniPrefs <Name>): the file name without .module, no spaces
Name=Template
; the list entry (default: Name)
Title=Template
; required: the module's own version, major.minor
Version=0.1
; the program started by the page's button, with PUBSCREEN=<screen>
Editor=SYS:Prefs/Template
; one to four headings, comma-separated: the usual ones are
;   AmigaOS, System, Display, Look, Menus & Desktop, Requesters,
;   Locale and time, Sound, Printing, Network, Datatypes
; any other name gets a heading of its own
Categories=Look
; optional, shown by the Updates page: who wrote the module, the original software it is based on
; ("-" for none), and one or two sentences of what it opens or sets
Author=Your Name
BasedOn=Template 1.0
Description=Opens the Template editor.
